2.5.4 Spatial differentials in quality of reporting age-sex data
The UNAAI was used to analyse regional and district differentials in the quality of the age data
reporting. Table 2.11 shows that the Western Region had the best quality age-sex data with an
AAI of 37.2 while the Eastern Region had the worst quality with an index of 78.5. The indices for
the Northern and Southern regions were 59.4 and 6.6 respectively.
The Western Area Urban district had the lowest AAI (37.2), thus having its data rated as
‘inaccurate’. The AAI for the rest of the districts were greater than 40, hence their age-sex data
was rated as ‘highly inaccurate’.  Nine out of the 14 districts had age-sex data with an AAI higher
than 60.  The districts of the Eastern region had the worst quality of age-sex data with their AAI
lying between 70 and 90. These are followed by districts in the Northern Region, while those of
the Eastern Region had the best - although the quality was also not accurate.
