3.3.2 Population of the districts
The Western Area Urban district (Freetown City) was the most populous district in the country in
2015, with a population of 1.1 million persons, contributing 14.9 per cent of the total population
(Table 3.1). Bonthe district was the least populous, with only 200,781 persons. Eight out of the 14
districts had a population of 500,000 persons or more, and these collectively contributed 70.9 per
cent of the total population.
